@baseUrl = https://license.example.invalid
@organizationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@requestId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@activitySnapshotId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@documentSnapshotId = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@requesterToken = replace-with-requester-delegated-token
@managerToken = replace-with-configured-manager-delegated-token
@securityToken = replace-with-configured-security-delegated-token

### Client must explicitly configure/connect the target first. Role/principal are never submitted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "target": "investigation", "durationMinutes": 60, "emergency": false, "reason": "Time-limited incident investigation" }

### Saved request list, no cloud call.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

### Selected saved request; use the requestId returned by creation. Missing/foreign request returns 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

### First configured approver, not requester. Use the current response version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 0, "reason": "Manager verified operational need" }

### Second distinct configured approver; stale or duplicate approval returns 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{securityToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 1, "reason": "Security verified scope and duration" }

### Requester-only activation after approvals, explicit consent and fresh client configuration checks.
# Queues a LIVE native Azure PIM / client-owned AWS human-session broker / GCP PAM operation.
# Provider and mapped human are server configuration, never caller-submitted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 2, "reason": "Explicitly activate approved incident access", "liveConsent": true }

### Reject an unactivated request instead; update version to the selected request. Not early cloud revocation.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{securityToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 1, "reason": "Operational need no longer exists" }

### Requester ends own grant OR either current configured authorized approver revokes (no second approval).
# Use the latest saved version; missing consent/stale version is 409, missing reason 400.
# Pending/unissued cancels with zero native calls. RevokeQueued/RevokeIssuing/RevokeOutcomeUnknown are NOT verified success.
# Security approver can still revoke saved exact targets after Disabled/disconnect or requester membership removal.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{securityToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 5, "reason": "Incident contained; terminate exact temporary grant", "liveConsent": true }

### AWS/GCP aliases use the same API, dual approvals and explicit activation.
# AWS broker HTTPS/auth and GCP native human OAuth mapping must already be configured by the client.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "target": "aws-investigation", "durationMinutes": 15, "emergency": true, "reason": "Bounded native human incident session" }

### Saved append-only audit, no cloud call.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/privileged-access/{{requestId}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Analyze selected saved snapshots. Requires ManageRemediations and inventory/finding access.
# Potential review events may queue client-configured SIEM/notification/ticket deliveries.
# Provider enum remains numeric for existing API compatibility (Azure=0, Aws=1, Gcp=2).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/security-analysis
Authorization: Bearer {{securityToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": 1,
  "accountId": "123456789012",
  "activitySnapshotId": "{{activitySnapshotId}}",
  "entitlementSnapshotId": "{{documentSnapshotId}}"
}
